WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.351
Idea. Imagine giving directions. To a friend you say, go to the park. To a robot you must say, turn left ninety degrees, move ten steps, stop. One is easy for people. The other is exact for the machine.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:25.642
A high-level language, like Python, uses English-like words. People can read and write it easily. Here, total equals a plus b, then print the total.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:40.087
A low-level language is close to the hardware. Assembly language uses short mnemonics like L D A, load, and A D D, add. Machine code is pure binary. Here is the same addition in assembly.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:56.351
Compare them. High-level code is easy to read and portable, so it runs on different computers once translated. Low-level code is written for one processor, but it can control the hardware directly, run fast and use little memory.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:12.253
Method. Decide which level the question asks about, and whether it wants a benefit, a drawback or a comparison. Pick one feature. To compare, give both sides with whereas. To explain, link the feature to the scenario.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:24.273
Low-level languages are often used for device drivers and embedded systems. High-level languages are used for most general applications, such as games and websites.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:40.192
Worked example. Here is a real question from Paper 1 in June 2025. A team writes smartwatch software in assembly language. Explain one benefit of writing it in a low-level language. Two marks.

00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:51.009
Recall the key benefit. Low-level code can directly access the hardware and the registers. So the programmers control exactly what the hardware does.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:02:01.327
Now link it to the device. A smartwatch has limited hardware: small memory and a small battery. So it must be used as efficiently as possible.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:18.016
So the answer is: programmers can make the best use of the smartwatch's limited hardware, because low-level code gives direct access to its hardware and registers. This explanation is by olevels.com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:28.685
Common mistake. A common mistake is saying high-level languages run faster, or that low-level ones are easier. It is the other way round.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:36.490
Another mistake is a vague word like better. Say how it is better, and in a compare question cover both sides.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:50.831
Your turn. Now you try. A team is writing a phone app that must run on many different types of phone. Should they use a high-level or a low-level language? Explain one reason. Pause and decide.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:03:04.252
Answer. High-level. High-level code is portable. The same source code can be translated to run on each type of phone, whereas low-level code only works on one type of processor.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:12.773
Remember the method: pick the level, pick one feature, and link it to the task. Now try the practice questions for this type.
